From efa046e21ae6968850c527473df9bb4a0af65847 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:06:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Offer to save the 3D correction into the file

The packing the person chose and the swap of the eyes are kept in the program's
own store, next to the resume position, and the file is never touched on its
own. When a correction is set, the video is shown in 3D and it is a file on
this computer, the 3D Video menu and the 3D Video Settings window offer to
save the correction into the file. The question comes first. On yes the
shared library of the stereo layer (libstereo-av, stereo_mark_save) writes it:
Matroska and WebM StereoMode (the depth layouts 15 to 20 included), MP4 and
MOV st3d. The file is read back; the stored choice is unmarked and the file is
read again as it is. A refusal says why and what to do, leaves the file as it
was and keeps the choice: a depth layout into MP4, a layout WebM cannot name, a
stream that declares its own layout, no room in an MP4 header, mkvpropedit
missing, a half or full size choice the shape of the video does not give.

Dragon without the library is built without the offer (the menu entry never
appears). A test of the writing and the refusals makes ffmpeg files and reads
them back.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
(cherry picked from commit eac9f9b0913b53aacf04aa1f2b4e7ebe6b6498c8)
